  "source_text": "During the evening-shift interview the driver explains that road signs sometimes appear as two overlapping images after several hours, improving when either eye is covered, although this did not occur during the short consultation; he reports no diplopia at rest, and the nurse has not established the angle from central fixation or whether the symptom persists with the updated lenses.\r\n\r\nA loose optometry slip lists right 6/12 and left 6/18 beside an earlier date and right 6/6 and left 6/9 beside a later date, but it does not identify which measurements were corrected; the driver describes a blurred patch off to one side, has no formal binocular field result, and has not supplied the specialist assessment.\r\n",
